## Configuration

[c12](https://github.com/unjs/c12) loads `{{kebabCase name}}.config.{ts,mts,js,mjs,json,...}` or
`.{{kebabCase name}}rc` from the working directory. `--config <file>` loads that file instead, and
fails if it does not exist. Invalid settings exit with code 3.

Configuration files import `defineConfiguration` for types:

```ts
// {{kebabCase name}}.config.ts
import { defineConfiguration } from "{{scope}}/{{kebabCase name}}";

export default defineConfiguration({
	verbose: true,
});
```

## Scripts

Run these from this directory, or from the repository root with
`node --run turbo -- run <script> --filter={{scope}}/{{kebabCase name}}`.

| Script | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `build` | Bundles `src/` into `dist/` with tsdown. |
| `lint` | Lints this package with the repository's oxlint, ESLint, and Biome configuration. |
| `test` | Runs the Vitest suite. |
| `type-check` | Type-checks this package and its references with `tsc --build`. |

